xara 0.1.3 -> 0.1.4: FM busy-channel detection no longer takes an open squelch's hiss for a station.

From yaesu-netradio (W5PL), 2026-11-27, https://github.com/jwheeler188/yaesu-netradio
xara is by x0rro (MIT licence); its repository was discontinued and emptied on 2026-11-08, so this fix is shared as a patch.

On FM, xara used its HF single-bin "carrier" test, which assumes flat noise. A real FM receiver's hiss with the squelch
open is tilted 15-20 dB across the passband; on an FT-897D xara held BUSY on 97 % of the time with nobody there, and
Pat waited for a clear channel for ever. On FM, xara now learns the receiver's hiss bin by bin and calls the channel
busy when the last 0.34 s differs from it by more than 2 dB across the band. Measured on that radio: hiss alone 0 %
busy; xara's VARA FM, narrow and wide, busy within 0.12-0.25 s, even 15 dB under the hiss. HF is unchanged.

Apply in the top folder of the xara 0.1.3 source:   patch -p1 < xara-0.1.4-fm-busy.patch
Then:   cargo test -p xara-phy --test busy fm_tilted     and build as usual.

